&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Agile Robots SE is an innovative company with a clear mission: bringing intelligent robotic solutions to our customers. We combine the latest technology in the field of AI with powerful robotic systems — from industrial robot arms and mobile manipulators to humanoids — to solve tasks that classical automation cannot address.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our solutions are deployed with international customers across a wide range of industries. Seamless integration and scalable deployment are at the core of our mission. Every one of these solutions starts as physical hardware — robotic workcells that we design, build, and commission in our own labs before they go into production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a passionate Senior Mechanical Engineer for Robotic Systems to turn robotics concepts into reliable physical systems. In this role, you will design the mechanical parts of our workcells, build and assemble them in our labs, and make sure they meet the relevant safety standards. You will own our lab infrastructure, tooling, and material, and be the hands-on partner for our robotics, software, and application engineers. The role is based in Munich, Germany.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design mechanical parts, fixtures, grippers, mounts, and enclosures for the robotic workcells in our labs and in customer projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate workcell and production line concepts in simulation — reachability, collisions, and cycle times — before any hardware is built&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Construct, assemble, and commission complete robotic workcells — from the frame and mounting concept to cabling and final integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain CAD models, technical drawings, and bills of materials, and prepare parts for manufacturing via CAM and 3D printing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build up a library of reusable mechanical modules, standard components, and design templates, and feed lessons learned from existing workcells back into it, so that each new cell is faster to design than the last&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the organization of our labs, including tools, equipment, material stock, and the procurement of mechanical components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that our workcells adhere to the relevant machine safety norms and support risk assessments, safeguarding concepts, and technical documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with robotics, software, and application engineers to translate application requirements into robust mechanical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to customer and deployment sites to support the installation, commissioning, and on-site adaptation of workcells (up to 20% of working time)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Essential Skills&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Mechanical Engineering, Mechatronics, or a related field — or equivalent practical experience, e.g. a technical apprenticeship with several years of relevant work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of four years of professional experience in mechanical design, machine building, or industrial automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid CAD skills (e.g., SolidWorks, Fusion 360, Inventor, Creo) for part and assembly design including technical drawings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with robot simulation and offline programming environments (e.g., RoboDK, RobotStudio, Visual Components)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with CAM and common manufacturing processes (milling, turning, sheet metal) as well as with 3D printing, including design for manufacturability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with aluminum profile systems, linear axes, fixtures, and standard mechanical components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with robotic hardware (robot arms, grippers, cameras, AGVs, sensors, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on mindset — you enjoy building, assembling, and commissioning hardware yourself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of machine safety norms and a structured approach to safe workcell design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured and independent working style with a strong sense of order in the lab&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Beneficial Skills&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of electrical engineering: wiring, control cabinets, and the integration of sensors and actuators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with pneumatics: valves, cylinders, vacuum grippers, and air supply&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with functional safety standards and safety equipment (e.g., EN ISO 10218, ISO/TS 15066, EN ISO 13849, safety scanners, light curtains, emergency stop circuits)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with external manufacturing suppliers and in procurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic programming skills (e.g., Python) or experience with PLC programming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German language skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;TranslationField-module__fieldItemName___Q0F_7 TranslationField-module__aboutUsWrapper___WXJpq&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;A dynamic high-tech company, combined with financial soundness and world-class investors.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Join an interdisciplinary, international team with 60+ different nationalities in a collaborative work environment.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Lots of development opportunities as we continue to grow.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Challenging tasks and impactful projects alongside experts that enable professional and personal growth.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Corporate Benefits Program covering health, mobility, and learning for 100€ net per month.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Modern office facilities with a rooftop terrace overlooking Munich, free drinks &amp;amp; fruits, and regular company events contribute to a good working environment&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;TranslationField-module__fieldItemValue___c0djd&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agile Robots SE&lt;/strong&gt; is an international high-tech company based in Munich, Germany with a production site in Kaufbeuren and more than &lt;strong&gt;3500&lt;/strong&gt; employees worldwide. Our mission is to bridge the gap between artificial intelligence and robotics by developing systems that combine state-of-the-art force-moment-sensing and world-leading image-processing technology. This unique combination of technologies allows us to provide user-friendly and affordable robotic solutions that enable intelligent precision assembly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is made possible by our employees, who bring out the best in each and every day with creativity and enthusiasm. Become part of this team and shape the future of robotics with us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud of our diversity and welcome your application regardless of gender and sexual identity, nationality, ethnicity, religion, age, or disability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Agile Robots SE is an innovative company with a clear mission: bringing intelligent robotic solutions to our customers. We combine the latest technology in the field of AI with powerful robotic systems — from industrial robot arms and mobile manipulators to humanoids — to solve tasks that classical automation cannot address.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the heart of our offering is a versatile software platform for orchestrating complex robotic systems. It allows efficient customization for specific customer requirements: configuring systems, developing reusable skills, parameterizing processes, and executing tasks reliably in production. Learned models — from perception to end-to-end policies — are a core part of this platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our solutions are deployed with international customers across a wide range of industries. Seamless integration and scalable deployment are at the core of our mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a passionate Forward Deployed AI Engineer to bring state-of-the-art robot learning and computer vision models into real production environments. In this role, you will train, fine-tune, and deploy AI models directly on customer robots — from Vision-Language-Action models and diffusion policies to perception and grasp generation networks. You will become a trusted technical partner, turning customer challenges into robust, data-driven robotics applications. The role is based in Munich, Germany.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy, fine-tune, and evaluate AI models on real robotic systems at customer sites — including Vision-Language-Action (VLA) models, diffusion policies, and other end-to-end learned policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adapt and train perception models for robotic applications, e.g. object detection, segmentation, and pose estimation based on YOLO, SAM, vision transformers, and self-supervised backbones such as DINOv2&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate and tune grasp generation models (e.g., GraspNet, Dex-Net, Contact-GraspNet) for bin picking and manipulation tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build data pipelines for customer deployments: demonstration and teleoperation recording, dataset curation, annotation, training runs, and systematic evaluation of model performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring models into production: optimize inference, deploy on edge and embedded hardware, and integrate models into our robotic software platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with customers to understand technical requirements and translate them into robust, AI-driven robotics applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose, troubleshoot, and resolve model, software, and system integration issues both remotely and on-site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to international customer sites for workshops, deployments, training, and technical support (up to 40% travel)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Essential Skills&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&#39;s degree in Robotics, Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, or a related field — or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of four years of professional experience in machine learning, AI for robotics, or computer vision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience working with real robots — robot arms, mobile manipulators, grippers, cameras, and sensors — not only in simulation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience with end-to-end learned models for robotics (e.g., VLAs, diffusion policies, imitation or reinforcement learning policies), covering training, fine-tuning, and deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills in both Python and C++&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid command of machine learning frameworks (e.g., PyTorch, TensorFlow) and the full model lifecycle: data curation, training, evaluation, and deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with modern computer vision models such as YOLO, SAM, vision transformers, and self-supervised backbones (e.g., DINOv2, CLIP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with learned grasp generation for manipulation (e.g., GraspNet, Dex-Net, or comparable approaches)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of robot (inverse) kinematics, coordinate transformations, and hand-eye calibration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in Linux environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to learn new technologies and adapt quickly in customer environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Beneficial Skills&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with large-scale demonstration data collection, teleoperation setups, and sim-to-real transfer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with robot learning simulation frameworks (e.g., NVIDIA Isaac Sim/Lab, MuJoCo, Gazebo)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of classical computer vision (e.g., OpenCV, PCL, camera calibration, point cloud processing)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience optimizing inference (e.g., TensorRT, ONNX, quantization) and deploying on NVIDIA embedded platforms (e.g., Jetson Orin, AGX, Xavier)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with MLOps tooling: experiment tracking, dataset versioning, and continuous training or evaluation pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Publications or open-source contributions in robot learning, manipulation, or computer vision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with industrial automation environments (e.g., PLCs, EtherCAT, OPC UA)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;TranslationField-module__fieldItemName___Q0F_7 TranslationField-module__aboutUsWrapper___WXJpq&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
